  "notes": "Warren J. Smith, Modern Lens Design, 2nd ed., Figure 16.13 (page number not visible in the photos). Book: EFL 100.6, BFL 17.37, NA -0.0621 (F/8.0), GIH 3.09 (HFOV=1.76), PTZ/F -4.5, VL 20.88, infinite conjugate. Glass: BK7 entered as N-BK7; KF9 entered as N-KF9. The book does not mark the stop; it is placed at surface 1, the front corrector. The table gives thicknesses without sign; spaces after an odd number of reflections are entered negative, which reproduces the book's VL. The table lists a Mangin mirror as entry surface, reflecting back surface and exit surface (the same physical surface twice); the reflecting surface is the one the light returns from. The secondary mirror is the aspheric rear surface of the corrector (surfaces 2 and 6). Conic constants (kappa) and aspheric terms (ad, ae, af, ag on r^4, r^6, r^8, r^10) as in the book. Central obscuration and baffles are not modelled.",
